        "id": 2379465696,
        "content": "1. Rate limiting for `uad.ubq.fi` was set up [this](https://developers.cloudflare.com/waf/reference/legacy/old-rate-limiting/#create-a-custom-rate-limiting-rule) way. Try to search for rate limiting rules in cloudflare dashboard:\r\n  a) `Security > WAF > Rate limiting rules`\r\n  b) In the \"Rules\" section of the `ubq.fi` domain settings\r\n<img width=\"1512\" alt=\"Screenshot 2024-09-27 at 17 47 30\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f3e6f320-1306-4a7a-b384-c1ce807f2d59\">\r\nI don't have permissions to view the rules in the cloudflare dashboard for your account.\r\n2. I've also accidentally found the redirect rule for the `ethcon.ubq.fi` subdomain. Perhaps try to move it higher in the UI so that it takes precedence over the `*.ubq.fi/*` rule.\r\n<img width=\"1512\" alt=\"Screenshot 2024-09-27 at 17 50 52\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6c13faef-bfdc-4e0f-acc4-20ee10eff52b\">",
